#{[17592186555782 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555782 #edb/ref 1069 "q-276631" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555782 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555782 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{2}{7-5x}.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$  \n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555782 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "306d067e-7a9d-57e7-9fd1-1469fa53a6b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555782 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{7-5x}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2}{7-5y}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2}{7-5y} \\\\ x(7-5y) & =2 \\\\ 7x-5xy & =2 \\\\ -5xy & =2-7x \\\\ 5xy & =7x-2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{7x-2}{5x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{7x-2}{5x}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555783 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555783 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148432" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555783 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555783 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{5}{2x-6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555783 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3136287b-ab52-50e3-8963-70ea96c4eb24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555783 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{2x-6}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{2y-6}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5}{2y-6} \\\\ x(2y-6) & =5 \\\\ 2xy-6x & =5 \\\\ 2xy & =6x+5 \\\\ y & =\\frac{6x+5}{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{6x+5}{2x}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555787 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555787 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148588" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555787 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555787 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x),$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3-kx}{x+1},\\,x\\ne -1\n$$\n\nhas an inverse function given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3-x}{x+4},\\,x\\ne -4.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555787 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "36115cd9-9382-506b-9404-8a68bbaccae0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555787 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3-kx}{x+1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3-ky}{y+1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3-ky}{y+1} \\\\ x(y+1) & =3-ky \\\\ xy+x & =3-ky \\\\ xy+ky & =3-x \\\\ y(x+k) & =3-x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3-x}{x+k}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3-x}{x+k}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555792 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555792 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148539" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555792 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555792 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x)=\\frac{3}{kx-2}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3+2x}{5x}.$ What is the value of $k?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555792 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3bd71fc1-9e9b-5a64-b8c7-ee650f7e3c32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555792 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3}{kx-2}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3}{ky-2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3}{ky-2} \\\\ x(ky-2) & =3 \\\\ kxy-2x & =3 \\\\ kxy & =3+2x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3+2x}{kx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3+2x}{kx}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555794 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555794 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148507" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555794 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555794 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=-\\frac{x-8}{5x+1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555794 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "411f5065-9d51-51d9-906e-20eb90eb5d15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555794 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{x-8}{5x+1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{y-8}{5y+1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{y-8}{5y+1} \\\\ -x & =\\frac{y-8}{5y+1} \\\\ -x(5y+1) & =y-8 \\\\ -5xy-x & =y-8 \\\\ 8-x & =5xy+y \\\\ 8-x & =y(5x+1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{8-x}{5x+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{8-x}{5x+1}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555803 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555803 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148504" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555803 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555803 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{2x-1}{x+3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555803 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "500aed1e-922d-582e-a7e3-3bbfcff68302" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555803 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2x-1}{x+3}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2y-1}{y+3}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2y-1}{y+3} \\\\ x(y+3) & =2y-1 \\\\ xy+3x & =2y-1 \\\\ 3x+1 & =2y-xy \\\\ 3x+1 & =y(2-x) \\\\ y & =\\frac{3x+1}{2-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3x+1}{2-x}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555809 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555809 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148499" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555809 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555809 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{3x+1}{x-4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555809 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "58d6a2d3-405c-5b5e-b02f-68804a6747aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555809 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3x+1}{x-4}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3y+1}{y-4}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3y+1}{y-4} \\\\ x(y-4) & =3y+1 \\\\ xy-4x & =3y+1 \\\\ xy-3y & =4x+1 \\\\ y(x-3) & =4x+1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{4x+1}{x-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{4x+1}{x-3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555818 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555818 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148433" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555818 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555818 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{6}{5x+3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555818 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6ad34a02-d412-58b2-a634-d74158ac441a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555818 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{6}{5x+3}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{6}{5y+3}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{6}{5y+3} \\\\ x(5y+3) & =6 \\\\ 5xy+3x & =6 \\\\ 5xy & =6-3x \\\\ y & =\\frac{6-3x}{5x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{6-3x}{5x}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555822 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555822 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148584" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555822 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555822 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x),$ defined as \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2x+k}{x-1},\\,x\\ne 1\n$$\n\nhas an inverse function given by \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x-8}{x-2},\\,x\\ne 2.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $k?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555822 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "754f4c4b-11dc-5f96-9fa9-3c28fe7e8a39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555822 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2x+k}{x-1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2y+k}{y-1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2y+k}{y-1} \\\\ x(y-1) & =2y+k \\\\ xy-x & =2y+k \\\\ xy-2y & =x+k \\\\ y(x-2) & =x+k \\\\ y & =\\frac{x+k}{x-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+k}{x-2}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=-8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555832 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555732 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555832 #edb/ref 1069 "q-276645" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555832 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555832 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{(4x+7)^{2}}$ is defined for $x>-\\frac{7}{4}.$ Find ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555832 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ea6de0b-579b-595d-b4da-dc4ce1abfbcc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555832 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{(4x+7)^{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{(4y+7)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{(4y+7)^{2}} \\\\ x(4y+7)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (4y+7)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\sqrt{(4y+7)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{x}} \\\\ |4y+7| & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ 4y+7 & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ 4y & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-7 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{7}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the fact that for $y>-\\frac{7}{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n|4y+7|=4y+7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{7}{4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555843 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555843 #edb/ref 1069 "q-276634" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555843 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555843 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{5}{6x+2}.$\n\n${f}^{-1}(x)=$  \n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555843 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a700c45d-e998-5eef-9aa2-096588d12ebe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555843 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5}{6x+2}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5}{6y+2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5}{6y+2} \\\\ x(6y+2) & =5 \\\\ 6xy+2x & =5 \\\\ 6xy & =5-2x \\\\ y & =\\frac{5-2x}{6x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5-2x}{6x}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555862 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555681 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555862 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148508" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555862 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555862 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=\\frac{5-2x}{x+1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555862 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de7ae964-9fce-58b0-bd1b-ba5303123396" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555862 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{5-2x}{x+1}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{5-2y}{y+1}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{5-2y}{y+1} \\\\ x(y+1) & =5-2y \\\\ xy+x & =5-2y \\\\ xy+2y & =5-x \\\\ y(x+2) & =5-x \\\\ y & =\\frac{5-x}{x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{5-x}{x+2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555865 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555865 #edb/ref 1069 "q-276781" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555865 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555865 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x)=\\frac{3k}{6+4x}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{9-6x}{4x}.$ What is the value of $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555865 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e33bcefe-71b8-5e01-9202-e30bde07e783" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555865 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{3k}{6+4x}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3k}{6+4y}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{3k}{6+4y} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3k}{6+4y} \\\\ x(6+4y) & =3k \\\\ 6x+4xy & =3k \\\\ 4xy & =3k-6x \\\\ y & =\\frac{3k-6x}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{3k-6x}{4x}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555872 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555872 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148537" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555872 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555872 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{7x+k}$ has an inverse function given by ${f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1+3x}{7x}.$ What is the value of $k?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555872 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa405f43-aa49-5df2-9659-18d1b520e384" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555872 #edb/ref 1074 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{7x+k}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{7y+k}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{7y+k} \\\\ x(7y+k) & =1 \\\\ 7xy+kx & =1 \\\\ 7xy & =1-kx \\\\ y & =\\frac{1-kx}{7x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1-kx}{7x}.\n$$\n\nComparing our answer with the given expression, we conclude that $k=-3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
